<title>USA: Shaw group cuts stake in Reynolds Metals.</title>
<headline>Shaw group cuts stake in Reynolds Metals.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by David E. Shaw and Co Inc said Tuesday it had lowered its stake in Reynolds Metals Co to 362,600 shares of seven percent PRIDES, or 3.3 percent of the total outstanding.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include net sales of 320,900 PRIDE shares between August 22 and September 5 at prices ranging from $47.25 to $48.5 per share.</p>
<p>A PRIDE is a preferred redeemable increased dividend equity security.</p>
</text>
